    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on exploiting favorable matchups against weaker arms, specifically targeting the start from Spence. **Kyle Tucker** (75.53) leads the charge as our most reliable asset; despite a modest -2% adjustment for potential stolen base suppression, his elite base projection remains unrivaled. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Andy Pages** (68.41) serve as the engines of today\u2019s offense. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive +19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile and a +14% dynamic platoon edge, while **Andy Pages** remains a high-floor play against the underwhelming Martinez. **Jackson Merrill** (65.98) and **Josh Jung** (63.35) round out a formidable core, both capitalizing on sub-5.00 xERA matchups that elevate their daily efficiency scores well into the \"Strong\" territory.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card involved the MI slot, where **Nasim Nunez** (59.76) edged out the rest of the bench depth. While his position at the bottom of the order carries a -8% penalty, his high sprint speed\u2014a priority given our scarcity strategy\u2014combined with the +19% SP skill advantage provided by Spence made him the preferred play over other utility options. **Curtis Mead** (62.15) continues to prove his worth in the 3-hole, bolstered by a +10% platoon boost, while **Wade Meckler** (53.39) remains a marginal start, saved from the bench only by the platoon advantage against Nelson. We continue to navigate the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, while **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are unavailable due to team off-days. Note that **Liam Hicks** faces the toughest test of the day against Wheeler (3.16 xERA); he remains in the lineup to preserve game caps, but his 43.67 score reflects the significant volatility inherent in facing an elite arm.",
